/////////////////
// make_blacksmith_items.src
//
// Use a smithy hammer to either repair arms & armor or
// to work with metal to create new items. You need to be
// skillful to work with the rarer metals.
//
// Author: DreamWeaver:
//	      original
//	 Racalac:
//	      colored items
// Updates: Dream Weaver 6/3/99 handled item quality an HP to new specs
//	  Ignatius     99/06/10 added name of maker to exceptional items.
//
// More Mods: DarkFyre 11/16/99 Added support for colored ores to be better/worse than normal
//		     also added name of maker to normal items so people can laugh at the
//		     really bad smiths ;)
//
// Even More Mods : Slaine 3/5/2002 Added craftable bone armour.
//
// 2026-08-30 -- OSI-style crafting gump, ported onto the shared
// pkg/systems/crafting/include/craftmenu framework (see bowcraft.src for the
// reference pattern). Replaces the old target-an-ingot-then-CreateMenu flow:
// the hammer now opens the gump directly (auto-detecting any ingot color
// from backpack + Omega Cache, with a picker like bowcraft's Log picker).
// Repair Item is still available as a gump Option, doing its own follow-up
// targeting step just like bowcraft/tailoring's Repair Item.
//
// Bone armor (the old Type-99/choice:=99 branch) is now just ordinary
// recipe entries in blacksmithy.cfg with a Material2Type "Bone" fixed slot
// plus CoSkillid/CoSkill (Tinkering, gating visibility only -- the original
// CanMakeBone never re-rolled Tinkering at craft time either, only Blacksmithy).
//
// Ore/ingot quality scaling (rarer ores are harder to work) is handled by
// craftmenu.inc's qualityDivider mechanism, reading Difficulty out of this
// same blacksmithy.cfg (see CraftMenu_GetFamilyQualityDifficulty).
////////////////

use uo;
use cfgfile;
use os;
use math;
use basicio;

include "util/repair";
include ":mdgumps:yesNo";
include "include/client";
include "include/objtype";
include "include/classes";
include "include/random";
include "include/itemutil";
include "include/autoloop";
include "include/attributes";
include "include/difficulty";
include ":crafting:craftingfunctions";
include "include/resourcemanager";
include ":karmafame:karmafame";
include ":crafting:craftmenu";
include "blacksmithgump";

// called when a player double-clicks a hammer or other blacksmith tool
program use_hammer( character, hammer )

	if( !ReserveItem( hammer ) )
		return;
	endif

	if( !NearForgeAndAnvil(character) )
		SendSysmessage( character , "You must be near a forge and an anvil to smith items!" );
		return;
	endif

	RunBlacksmithGump( character );

endprogram

// True if character is standing next to an anvil (mundane, elven, or soulforge).
// NearAnvil() replaced by craftingfunctions.inc's NearForgeAndAnvil() -- OSI-style
// dual forge+anvil requirement, shared with every Blacksmithy station entry point.
//
// 2026-09-12 -- MakeBlacksmithItems moved into blacksmithgump.inc alongside
// RunBlacksmithGump (crafting-station rollout): the Large Forge's Bellows
// animate script (pkg/items/forge/use.src) opens the same gump via that .inc
// without including this .src (which it can't -- this file has a program
// block), and the full pick-a-recipe flow ends in MakeBlacksmithItems, so it
// has to live somewhere both files can reach.
